# Corpus data (public/data/) is produced by the data pipeline (or the
# placeholder generator for local dev). It IS committed to version control
# (deliberately not gitignored) because the GitHub Actions Pages workflow
# (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) builds from a fresh `git checkout` on every
# push and has no other way to obtain it -- there is no CI step that reruns
# the multi-hour embedding pipeline. This is a considered exception: the
# corpus is synthetic (iamkaikai/amazing_logos_v2, see docs/DATASET.md) and
# its public deployment -- with prominent disclosure that it is not real
# trademark data -- has been explicitly decided as acceptable. Only the
# already-quantized/derived artifacts (index.bin, metadata.json,
# model_params.json, thumbnails/*.jpg) are committed here; the raw corpus
# download and full-precision intermediate embeddings
# (data-pipeline/raw/, data-pipeline/embeddings/) remain excluded via the
# root .gitignore and are never committed.

